<title>USA: Northrop awarded $262 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Northrop awarded $262 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp on Thursday said it was awarded a $262 million contract to upgrade Airborne Warning and Control Sytem radars by prime contractor Boeing Co.</p>
<p>The award follows NATO's recent decision to retrofit 17 E-3A AWACS aircraft with upgrades. As well as the 17 NATO planes the award includes upgrades for seven British planes, four U.S. planes and three ground-based radar support systems, one each for NATO, the U.S. and the U.K.  First delivery to Boeing as prime contarctor is expected by September.</p>
<p>The modifications will improve the system's ability to detect small objects and simplify operation and maintenance.</p>
</text>
